  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:24:09.934Z",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nWhat was the deadline and requirement for an individual to file the annual income tax return for the taxable year 2023?\n\n### Short Answer\nThe deadline for an individual to file the annual income tax return for the taxable year 2023 is on or before April 15, 2024. This requirement is stipulated under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Accounting Treatment\nFor accounting purposes, individuals must ensure that their income is accurately reported for the preceding taxable year. This includes all sources of income, which should be documented and reconciled with the amounts reported in the income tax return.\n\n### Tax Treatment\nUnder Section 51 of the NIRC, individuals are required to file an income tax return if they are Filipino citizens residing in the Philippines, Filipino citizens residing outside the Philippines on income from sources within the Philippines, or aliens residing in the Philippines on income derived from sources within the Philippines. The return must be filed with any authorized agent bank, Revenue District Officer, or through an authorized Tax Software provider.\n\n### Differences and Reconciliation\nThe primary difference in filing requirements may arise for individuals receiving purely compensation income from a single employer, who may not be required to file an annual income tax return if their tax has been withheld correctly. In such cases, the certificate of withholding serves as a substituted filing.\n\n### Practical Note\nTaxpayers should prepare their income tax returns well in advance of the April 15 deadline to ensure compliance and avoid penalties. It is advisable to gather all necessary documentation, including income statements and withholding certificates, to facilitate accurate reporting.",
